  "unlabelled_and_generality_review": [
    "A.1-A.2 establish embedded closed subgroups and quotient topology without assuming the theorem in the exponential prerequisite. Countable compact slices and an internal nested-ball argument prove transitive surjectivity of the differential. Discrete, zero-dimensional and disconnected groups are included.",
    "B gives both bundle-construction directions, full isotropy rather than infinitesimal equivariance, smooth descent, all principal axioms, curvature at arbitrary frames and flatness equivalence. C includes arbitrary disconnected K,L,G over a connected base, nonclosed holonomy, both algebra inclusions and the separate limitation concerning discrete components.",
    "C.2 proves the general reductive canonical connection for any isotropy homomorphism and the principal-L special case. D gives every integer Hopf weight including zero and negatives, exact curvature normalization, both holonomy groups, noncommutative rectangle transport, isotropy-induced circle monodromy and the reflection obstruction.",
    "E includes injectively immersed patches with their own topology, nondirect sums, singular orbits, local minimal dimension and the equivalence of base-orbit coverage. Both reduced-data conditions and smooth reconstruction on the whole bundle are proved, without properness or constant orbit dimension.",
    "F.1 explicitly proves equality of Q-stabilizer graphs equivalent to common H and lambda; thus it retains the historical hypothesis rather than assuming a stronger special case. The minimal-dimension direct sum, patchwise constant stabilizer action and all three reduced constraints are checked, including disconnected H.",
    "F.2-F.3 include the converse gauge gluing proof for every group element, the inverse adjoint with the stated section convention, and the common orbit-closure argument using openness of the principal projection.",
    "F.4 explicitly proves the full action-map diffeomorphism and its smooth inverse for arbitrary complementary translation spaces, as well as all potentials, full principal forms, curvature and the exact additive rectangle. F.5 generalizes the cubic counterexample to every nonzero Lie algebra and checks its compatibility even at the singular parameter.",
    "F.6 treats both nonexistence and every-connection gauge cases on an arbitrary base. F.7 proves the upper-triangular obstruction directly for the full specified principal bundle. F.8 covers arbitrary G and n>=1, both punctured radial and angular data, and necessity and sufficiency of zero data for extension.",
    "F.9 covers every smooth principal lift on a trivial bundle, derives its cocycle and its differential contribution, and proves necessity, sufficiency and the exact reduced-data correspondence. No arbitrary extra symmetry-direction term remains.",
    "G proves arbitrary smooth jets and the full even-function extension to all real arguments, with one-sided derivative estimates, flat remainder gluing and odd/quadratic division. Uniqueness is only on nonnegative squared radius. H proves the SU(2) covering and both Lie bracket normalizations without an external representation theorem.",
    "H.2 proves all smooth rotational connections including zero, with correct uniqueness and double-bracket conversion. H.3 includes the full curvature, not only its origin value. H.4 treats both SO(3) and SU(2) Euclidean groups and both lifts. H.5 distinguishes continuity and smoothness; H.6 proves the nonzero flat example, every coefficient and all origin constants."
  ],
